# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — 2026-10-21 11:22:50 UTC

## Current server-free gate results

Code revision: `da6345bb` (`test(remoting): cover recent admin header decode
modes`). It is followed only by documentation and execution-log commits in
this gate refresh.

- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` passed in 2m11s, including 37
  scenario-manifest cases, 80 Java-decoded Rust typed header frames, and 15
  typed body frames.
- The differential comparator self-test and 37-row manifest validation
  passed. The pinned Unique ID test passed under `TZ=Asia/Taipei`.
- `cargo run -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --example fuzz_smoke --locked`
  passed with 133 frame seeds, 11 message seeds, 2,304 bounded mutations,
  189 frame decodes, and 116 message decodes.
- `bash tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh` passed all 16 selected race/leak
  cases × 3 repetitions.
- Release facade examples built. The offline benchmark compiled, ran, and its
  measured output was appended to
  `docs/compatibility/PHASE_18_OFFLINE_BENCHMARK_BASELINE.md`. Strict
  all-feature benchmark Clippy passed.
- `scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py` passed. `cargo package --list` showed
  both `LICENSE` and `NOTICE` in each of the seven product packages.
- Release-checklist current-revision rows were appended for P18-V02 and the
  local P18-V03 preparation review. The checklist does not claim publication,
  release compatibility, or completion of the broad audit.

## Evidence still open

The complete P18-V01 source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow/reverse-export
reconciliation remains open. A read-only remote-head check found no branch
`phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`; the latest Actions runs listed are
from 2026-10-15 and do not exercise this revision. Therefore current-revision
Ubuntu/native-Windows P18-V04 CI evidence is unavailable here. The local
server-free gates pass without Docker or a Broker, and the 37-row Phase 19
handoff manifest validates; live Broker/Docker scenarios remain Phase 19 work.

The four pre-existing Phase 19 worktree paths remain unstaged and untouched.
